{"h":0.01181044870493364,"text":"exams and tests.","x":0.55555555968824666,"y":0.11028257451606327,"w":0.12551439921061203},{"text":"SHOW WHAT YOU KNOW","w":0.21193415323893233,"x":0.41152263708080822,"h":0.011773940345368938,"y":0.16562009402310141},{"x":0.4074074073498698,"w":0.010288065804375579,"y":0.18895348828919412,"h":0.0087209301803325978,"text":"1"},{"h":0.011627906907110019,"y":0.18749999984101862,"x":0.43415637588694406,"w":0.47530863444010413,"text":"Complete the table with the words in the box. Think about more"},{"text":"words to add to each group. Compare with a partner.","x":0.43415637444065347,"h":0.013081394896215404,"y":0.20203488372921785,"w":0.3930041164822049},{"text":"2","h":0.010174418169437871,"y":0.35319767450903106,"x":0.40740740754000188,"w":0.0123456785413954},{"x":0.44238683220606667,"h":0.013081394896215293,"w":0.17489712185329864,"text":"Chemistry coursebook","y":0.22674418618197956},{"x":0.62345679036947288,"y":0.2267441862970474,"w":0.24897118462456602,"text":"desk Geography head teacher","h":0.013081394896215293},{"h":0.013111058359430494,"text":"IT (Information technology) form teacher","x":0.44032921736408498,"y":0.23979591811483991,"w":0.30246914333767366},{"text":"IWB (interactive whiteboard) Maths PE (Physical Education)","y":0.25581395342628999,"w":0.44650204128689236,"x":0.4403292337118348,"h":0.011627906907110019},{"x":0.44032921746606818,"text":"Physics pupil Science whiteboard","w":0.27366255018446178,"h":0.013138439441962357,"y":0.26883830429974998},{"y":0.2978806908794065,"text":"Classroom objects","x":0.43621399375473874,"w":0.13374485439724398,"h":0.011773940345368938},{"x":0.43415637929844753,"y":0.31686046512917843,"text":"whiteboard","w":0.078189298841688348,"h":0.0087209301803323758},{"x":0.59869790680795554,"w":0.065978673299153634,"y":0.29779343709358508,"text":"Subjects","h":0.013424753581336102},{"x":0.75918843168625905,"y":0.29781914136812482,"w":0.053639598422580259,"text":"People","h":0.013373344996286174},{"y":0.35319767466914032,"w":0.46707817925347223,"h":0.013081394896215404,"text":"Finish the statements to make them true for you. Compare with","x":0.43415637583965655},{"x":0.43409072605003368,"text":"a partner.","w":0.07214776780870219,"y":0.36894883853435156,"h":0.010648834462068546},{"y":0.3850078492439617,"w":0.19341562906901044,"h":0.011794476157267808,"text":"1 My favourite subject is ...","x":0.43415638165891046},{"y":0.39952904237517628,"h":0.011808166698533684,"x":0.43415637609206892,"w":0.16872428046332466,"text":"2 My worst subject is ..."},{"w":0.27366255018446178,"y":0.41405023537435581,"h":0.011821857614082942,"text":"3 The best thing about my school is ...","x":0.43415638378979921},{"x":0.43415639114821097,"y":0.42877906980225888,"text":"4 The worst thing about my school is ...","h":0.01162790690711013,"w":0.28189298841688365},{"x":0.41563786100823041,"text":"UK TODAY","w":0.16666666666666663,"h":0.018954674527633886,"y":0.47959183678387918},{"y":0.51648351702592898,"w":0.44705881754557292,"text":"Education in Britain","h":0.037683148586207249,"x":0.41176471446250745},{"y":0.56104651157551477,"x":0.4176954893686502,"text":"The text describes the school system in England and Wales. Scotland","h":0.011627906907110019,"w":0.48148145887586802},{"text":"and Northern Ireland have different systems.","y":0.57692307683527411,"w":0.31687242296006951,"x":0.41563786655494456,"h":0.010286225254531933},{"x":0.41563787361653642,"y":0.59447674414818907,"h":0.011627906907110019,"w":0.49382714165581593,"text":"In England and Wales nowadays many children go to nursery school"},{"text":"when they are three or four. When they are five, they go to primary","h":0.013081394896215293,"x":0.41563786819453802,"y":0.60901162835131095,"w":0.47942386203342019},{"x":0.41769549047362592,"y":0.62354651163619468,"w":0.47325100368923606,"h":0.013081394896215293,"text":"school and they stay there for six years. At the age of eleven, they"},{"text":"start secondary school. Students have to study between the ages of","y":0.63953488401121128,"w":0.48971191406250003,"h":0.010174418169437871,"x":0.41769547840084886},{"h":0.01162790690711013,"x":0.4156378684156376,"w":0.49999999999999994,"y":0.65406976737977829,"text":"five and eighteen. Most students study at the same secondary school"},{"w":0.4917695448133681,"h":0.011627906907110019,"x":0.41563786748529119,"y":0.66860465112493328,"text":"for seven years, but some leave school at the age of sixteen and, for"},{"y":0.68313953491853796,"h":0.011627906907110019,"text":"example, study at college or train for a job for two more years.","w":0.45267486572265619,"x":0.41769549649395282},{"x":0.41769547650061073,"y":0.7020348837557473,"h":0.011627906907110019,"text":"At the age of eighteen or nineteen students can go to university,","w":0.46090535481770839},{"text":"which usually lasts three or four years.","x":0.4156378723500192,"y":0.71656976747667755,"w":0.28395060221354168,"h":0.011627906907110019},{"w":0.50823042127821183,"x":0.41769549741987877,"text":"Some parents pay for their children to go to a private school, but most","y":0.73390894808528306,"h":0.011773940345368938},{"text":"students go to state schools. Most state schools are mixed - they are","w":0.49794236924913193,"h":0.011773940345368938,"x":0.41769547621219694,"y":0.74999999985433208},{"x":0.41563787385280015,"y":0.76452119315634193,"h":0.011773940345368938,"w":0.49794236924913193,"text":"for boys and girls - but some are single-sex for either boys or girls only."},{"text":"Exams","x":0.4176954741868158,"y":0.7877906977902811,"w":0.059670778910319022,"h":0.010174418169437871},{"w":0.5,"text":"There are different types of exams in British schools. All students have","h":0.011799039795784227,"x":0.41769547825102865,"y":0.80651491359963134},{"h":0.011812730337050104,"y":0.82103610675022576,"x":0.41563786860299312,"text":"to study English, Maths and Science until Year Eleven. At the end of","w":0.47530863444010418},{"text":"that year, at the age of sixteen, students take GCSE exams*. Students","h":0.013748939969288831,"y":0.83523741466469403,"x":0.41558141929110864,"w":0.48776438395182292},{"x":0.41563785383853391,"y":0.85164835159235008,"w":0.48765431722005204,"h":0.011773940345368938,"text":"usually take GCSEs in five to ten subjects, so they have to revise a lot"},{"h":0.011773940345368938,"text":"before their exams. If students want to go to university, they take","x":0.41769547707710408,"w":0.45679012722439238,"y":0.86616954465089047},{"w":0.48971191406250003,"h":0.011773940345368938,"text":"A level exams*. Most students take two or three A levels, but some do","x":0.41769548720743299,"y":0.88069073767429451},{"h":0.011773940345368827,"x":0.41563787599109697,"w":0.47736623128255212,"text":"four. If students don't pass their exams or don't do well and get bad","y":0.89521193101021912},{"x":0.41563786174500611,"h":0.011773940345368938,"y":0.91130298280349276,"text":"marks, they can always retake the exams.","w":0.3004115125868056},{"text":"GCSE exams (GCSEs) - General Certificate of Secondary Education","h":0.010331860516846092,"y":0.94767441876775205,"x":0.41563787843866523,"w":0.41358022054036453},{"h":0.010293070525164927,"x":0.41563787215490772,"y":0.95918367339967037,"w":0.39094648573133678,"text":"A level exams (A levels) - Advanced Level (end-of school exams)"}]